\description{
Submits the selection as an export (\code{POST /exports}): the API writes
\strong{every record} of the selection, up to \code{limits$max_export_observations}
observations (10,000,000; \code{\link[=soil_capabilities]{soil_capabilities()}}), into a zip of files,
then keeps it for 7 days. Exports are the way to large selections: the
synchronous reads (\code{\link[=soil_observations]{soil_observations()}}, \code{\link[=soil_features]{soil_features()}}) are refused
above \code{limits$max_sync_observations} (1,000,000). Rule of thumb: size the
selection with \code{\link[=soil_summary]{soil_summary()}}; below about 200,000 observations read
synchronously, above it export (a whole-WoSIS wide CSV export takes about
9 minutes on the server, 88 MB zipped). Exports also give GeoPackage and
Shapefile files for GIS.
